WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:03.760
Remain vigilant at all times!

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.120
All soldiers, prepare to sortie!

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:08.960
Yes Sir!

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.300
After Fouzen was taken down, the situation has become dire.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.270
To think General Gregor fell so easily...

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.750
Indeed.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.430
But when you consider that his opponent was <i>that</i>  Squad 7, it's not too surprising, is it?

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.430
Welkin Gunther.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.210
Our front lines are being pushed back.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:31.000
Moreover, we lost Fouzen.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.210
We've lost the ability to wage a long-term war.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.600
Isn't it time for us to show some power?

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.650
You don't have to remind me.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.920
The next operation is being planned.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.630
Your worries are unnecessary.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.970
When the time is ripe, you'll know about it, even if you don't wish to.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.660
Before that happens, just wait.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.380
What's this? Keeping secrets from me?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.220
Umm... General Jaeger?

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:04.940
What is it?

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.890
May I ask you something?

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:07.770
Yeah.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.440
What kind of relationship do they have?

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.860
Why're you asking? You...

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.850
Ah, no, it's not like...

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.240
How do I put it... Well...

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.770
I don't know the details,

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:25.700
but their relationship shouldn't be as simple as it seems.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.100
Selvaria...

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.350
That's my name.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:43.840
And...

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.110
it's also the name of these blue roses.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.010
You showed me the place where I belonged.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.030
It has been a while since we've admired flowers together like this.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.480
It reminds me of the past.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.230
Your Highness...

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.440
Being able to stand under this sun today,

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.280
and being able to accompany you...

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.130
I owe all these to your benevolence.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.540
At that time,

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:50.060
ever since you cut the chains which bound me...

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.780
Come.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.660
...I've been living my future for your sake alone.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.990
Chapter 16

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.990
Unexpressed Feelings

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.960
Damn! Why did I...

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.440
Um...

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.480
T-Thanks!

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.940
W-Well, I have other things to take care of, so...

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.560
Seriously,

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.540
why is everyone so...

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:16.520
Yo, commander!

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:18.740
Largo.

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:19.960
Are you all right?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.210
I'm asking if you're all right.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.300
If there's a problem, I can-

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.410
Thanks.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.630
But I'm all right.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.600
Sorry for making you worry.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.690
I have a conference, so I have to go.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:36.750
Later.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.150
In this world, only those who have problems...

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.450
...say that they're all right.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:56.560
I... like you.

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:06.590
Uh... I... I...

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:32.550
Where's the fire?

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.490
Huh, Alicia?

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.610
What are you doing?

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:40.910
I was... making bread...

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.090
How are your squad members?

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:46.020
Yeah, they're all fired up.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.180
Judging from your look, you must be facing a lot of problems.

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.300
Faldio.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.370
Well, a lot's happened.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.660
Please.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:58.230
It would be troublesome if your absent-mindedness
 results in Alicia being hurt.

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:07.560
After our success at Fouzen, the tides have shifted in our favor.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.470
The Imperial Army should be planning how to end this war quickly,

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.750
since it will be difficult for them to obtain resources.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:18.500
We must observe the movements of the anxious Imperial Army,

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:21.700
and act carefully at the same time.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:22.520
That's all.

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.710
Welkin, I'm leaving first.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:32.290
2nd Lieutenant Gunther.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:33.300
Yes.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.070
Don't lose focus.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:36.040
Yes Ma'am!

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.720
My utmost apologies.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:39.680
Excuse me.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:51.290
Largo, is something wrong?

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:53.760
I should be the one asking you that!

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.450
Let's take a walk.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.450
Where are we going?

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.140
Don't worry about it.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.670
I know the best place for a good chat.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.110
A tent?

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.620
Well, take a look inside.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:16.500
Okay.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.840
This is...

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.940
This is called heart-to-heart.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.110
In my pocket~

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:41.160
There's a radish flower~

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:45.330
That girl's smile which I secretly sought~

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:51.070
I hold it in my heart~!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.120
The army gets things like these?

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.530
Squads that produce results are treated differently.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.000
They have benefits to the allocation of resources.

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.850
Is it really okay? We're the only ones using it. {THEN WHY ARE U USING IT?!}

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:05.720
Nah, we just happened to come in first.

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.610
There's no problem.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.030
So what did you want to talk about?

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:14.410
Well, it's just...

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:18.740
A lot of things don't go well in our lives.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:23.950
You're a veteran commander, but you're still a recruit down there?

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.670
I can tell just by looking.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.970
You guys aren't doing too hot, right?

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:30.930
Wait, what are you talking about...

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.740
More importantly, who are you talking about?

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.260
I'm not really...

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.030
Don't be shy.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:41.770
It's fine as long as there's no problem with Squad 7 as a whole.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:47.800
There's something like this which happened in the past.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.610
It's a story from the previous war.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.030
There was a new recruit.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:09:00.130
At that time, he was just a greenhorn.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:05.530
Dead set on protecting his country, he joined the militia and picked up a rifle.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:12.580
Back then, he was only focused on the fighting.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:18.920
However...

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:19.860
Largo!

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:25.060
The man who had nothing made a friend,

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:28.150
a brother-in-arms on the battlefield.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.270
He even found a woman he liked.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:32.130
Oh, really?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.040
What's wrong?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.470
Hey, Largo.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.570
Let me introduce you. This is my good friend Largo.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:45.540
This is Private First-Class Eleanor Varrot, who just joined the militia today.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.790
Pleased to meet you.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.390
L-Likewise.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:55.450
Although the man had never fallen seriously in love with a woman before,

00:09:55.450 --> 00:10:00.050
he tried his best in his own way, in spite of his clumsiness.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:03.760
The guy was just too clumsy though.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:08.370
He didn't really know how to get close to her.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:13.400
Perhaps, for him, that was even harder than fighting in battle.

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:19.110
But he always thought: "Today I talked to her" or...

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.390
"Today she talked to me".

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:25.240
He got happy over such small things.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:34.290
Well, after that, it was the usual.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:38.090
She didn't think he was too bad, either.

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:40.800
Did he confess his love?

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.720
No, he couldn't.

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.810
Why?

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.970
Just when he was about to confess,

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:52.520
he realized that his best friend liked her too.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.490
His best friend was smart and suave;

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.780
a trustworthy man.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.980
He was saved by that friend many times on the battlefield.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:05.740
If you consider it from her point of view, they were definitely more suited for each other.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.300
But even then...

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:10.030
Of course, he gave it some serious thought.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:12.750
To choose between friendship or his own feelings.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:16.880
Did he give up just like that?

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.690
I don't know. But before he came to a real conclusion, his best friend died.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:26.830
From the end result, it seemed that he had chosen friendship.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:30.680
Too much things happened then.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:36.400
I wonder if the woman noticed?

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:37.110
Huh?

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.110
Although death is a very sad thing,

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:42.570
there's no need for everyone to be unhappy.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:46.460
Things probably became like this because she knew.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:48.730
Eleanor isn't that stupid...

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.330
By Eleanor, you mean that Captain Varrot-

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.460
Idiot, don't tell anybody that!

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.670
Or I'll hunt you down!

00:11:57.670 --> 00:12:01.910
I don't plan to say anything, but you said everything yourself...

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.290
Anyway!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.920
What I want to say is:

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:10.350
Commander, you shouldn't follow in my footsteps.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:14.600
Yeah. Thanks, Largo.

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:21.100
Okay.

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:21.900
Go ahead.

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.140
Hop on!

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:40.390
Why?

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.720
Well, you wanted to go somewhere right?

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:47.260
Even so, I don't think that I need a ride from you.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:50.280
I-I see. Forget it then.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.510
I lied.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.560
Can you take me to the market?

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.490
O-Okay.

00:12:58.490 --> 00:13:00.890
But, is it all right? I thought you said that you didn't need a ride?

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:04.650
Although I don't need a ride, this is more relaxing.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.070
Oh, I see.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:07.530
Let's go then.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.660
Okay, then I'm counting on you, Ramal.

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.390
Is something the matter?

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.070
You said my name just now.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.330
It's your imagination.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.780
Please hurry up and drive.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:22.130
O-Okay.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:09.630
Thank you for shopping with me today.

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:12.080
O-Oh, I was free anyway.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.390
Don't mention it.

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:15.620
Speaking of which,

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.260
you sure bought a lot.

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:20.670
What are you going to do with so many things?

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.750
My brother seems to be quite depressed recently,

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.330
so I want to cheer him up.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:28.220
You're incredible.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.950
It's a given.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:32.240
He's my only family after all.

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:36.040
But you shouldn't be worrying about others, right?

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.850
Earlier, you...

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:41.310
I'm fine. Things like that always happen.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.170
You're strong.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.450
I'm just used to it.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:49.380
I'm not strong or anything.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:51.590
But,

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.940
if my wish can come true...{SHE FINALLY TALKS ABOUT HER WISH!}

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:59.820
I just hope the world can become a place where people openly admit their mistakes.

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:06.260
Yeah.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:18.330
Faldio is a good person.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.000
But...

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.360
Why?

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:37.770
Argh, enough!

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:40.890
It's so unlike me to think so much!

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:43.850
I have to make things clear!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:57.530
All right!

00:15:58.190 --> 00:15:59.240
Welkin!

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:00.780
W-What?

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.830
I have something to talk to you about.

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.130
Um...

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.770
What did you want to talk about?

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:24.400
Things have become kind of weird between us lately.

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.610
It feels unnatural.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.040
Y-Yeah.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:32.140
Why did it become like this?

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:33.650
You're right.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:35.650
I find it strange too.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.350
I don't like this.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.390
You're my direct superior.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:45.260
I think we're going to be fighting together even more, too.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.760
I'm sorry.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:50.250
I made you feel awkward.

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.630
No...

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.730
I don't want your apology.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:58.030
I just want to chat with you normally, like before.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.310
Welkin, what about you?

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:05.550
Me too.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:09.710
I don't want things to continue like this either.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:10.730
That's great.

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.200
I thought you had started to dislike me.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.780
Why would I?

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:19.040
Actually, I think of you as-

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:20.560
Oh, it's not-

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:22.490
How should I say it...

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:26.710
Well...

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:29.200
You're my precious...

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:32.380
You're my precious...

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:33.590
...friend.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:39.010
Alicia?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.180
Let's patch things up then.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.850
Yeah.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:48.520
With this, Faldio won't have to worry anymore.

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:52.850
Why?

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:57.050
Why do you have to mention Faldio at a time like this?

00:17:57.050 --> 00:18:00.250
Because he... seems worried.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:03.680
This is a problem between you and me, right?

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.960
It has nothing to do with Faldio, right?

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:09.160
Faldio confessed to me.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.790
What should I do?

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.640
W-Well...

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.250
Faldio is a good guy.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:20.130
That's not what I'm asking!

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:23.060
I want to know how you feel!

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:25.340
Even if you ask me something like that...

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.550
"Something like that?"

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:29.560
This should be a problem between you and Faldio, right?!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:32.770
You shouldn't ask for my opinion.

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:38.870
<i>The joys of being loved,</i>

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:35.530
Do you really think so?

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.450
You're fine with this?

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:45.650
<i>along with my unchanging life,</i>

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.700
I get it.

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:52.800
<i>become engraved into my memories.</i>

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:59.430
<i>Yet I always remember that one love.</i>

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:07.370
<i>No matter how far away tomorrow may be,</i>

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:12.870
<i>I have the strength to believe.</i>

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:22.910
<i>Love chains were born in my heart that day...</i>

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:27.770
<i>T'was the light which connected us.</i>

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:37.260
<i>They continue to echo-</i>

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:42.230
<i>Love Chains</i>

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.240
Welcome back, Brother.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:59.870
I haven't made these in a while, so...

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:03.240
Looks like I botched it a little.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:08.740
I'm home.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:12.840
My name is Isara.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.430
My name is just Isara.

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:17.950
Darcsens don't have surnames.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:21.850
That's why, when I was adopted into the Gunther family,

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:24.240
I had an indescribable feeling.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.110
My brother said that this is what a family feels like.

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:30.040
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles,

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:33.480
Chapter 17: Gifts from the Spirits.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.170
If fate is decided when we're born,

